# Cloudflare — egress this entry needs.
#
# Allowlist syntax, so what you read here is what lands in the deployment's
# /etc/agent-allowlist. Uncommented lines are what the provider needs to work;
# anything below the OPTIONAL marker is off until you turn it on.
#
# METHODS is not optional in practice. Omitting it defaults the entry to
# GET,HEAD,OPTIONS, and a wrangler deploy is a PUT — so a bare
# `api.cloudflare.com` line blocks deployment while looking right.

api.cloudflare.com      GET,POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — nothing below is needed for the provider to work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.workers.dev           GET,POST    # reach your own deployed Worker to test it
#
# That line is the sharpest illustration in the bank of why this file is not
# `hosts`. `*.workers.dev` is fine to make REACHABLE — the worst case is the
# agent talking to a stranger's Worker with no credential attached. It would be
# a serious bug in `hosts`, because anyone can register a workers.dev name and
# an injection match there hands them a live Cloudflare token. The repo enforces
# that asymmetry: `injection_wildcard_multitenant` in scripts/lib/invariants.sh
# fails on exactly this suffix, and only for addons that attach a credential.
